determinismo: time namespaces with a realtime offset, changeable while tasks are in them

A node's clock skew (the clock_skew fault): CLOCK_REALTIME, CLOCK_REALTIME_COARSE and
CLOCK_TAI offset per time namespace, read through the vDSO (its offsets, and time()) or the
syscalls (clock_gettime, gettimeofday, time), absolute deadlines on them converted to the
host's (clock_nanosleep, timers, timerfd, futex waits), set through
/proc/<pid>/timens_offsets ("realtime <sec> <nsec>") at any time.

